        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@xzbdmw, @niveK77pur: I finally decided to resolve #568 and the only good way to do it was indeed with introducing limit on scope computation. I decided to go with strict line count restriction (as in 'mini.ai' and 'mini.surround') which makes scope marked as \"incomplete\".\n\nAs scopes with incomplete computations usually contain information which is actively harmful for drawing (as it usually covers text), those should not be drawn. To achieve that, I decided to go a bit more generic route and introduce `config.draw.predicate` which can be used to decide whether scope needs to be drawn. This also should resolve this issue with config which looks something like this:\n\n```lua\nlocal draw_predicate = function(scope)\n  return not scope.body.is_incomplete and (scope.body.bottom - scope.body.top + 1) >= 3\nend\nrequire('mini.indentscope').setup({ draw = { predicate = draw_predicate } })\n```",
